            <div xml:id="d585">

                <pb facs="0739" n="643" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg643"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.6363 Standard Oil/30: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Persia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Engert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Teheran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-09-04T22:00:00+03:25"><hi rendition="#italic">September 4,
                                1921—10 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received September 7—10:15
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>52. British Minister tells me confidentially that his Government has instructed
                    him to protest against Russian oil concessions being transferred to American
                    concern.</p>
                <p>I am also informed that French interests are seeking the same concessions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
